{
  "_comment": [
    "The Age's own rings, arching overhead from horizon to horizon and never moving, lit by the sun and crossed by the planet's shadow at night: bright, broad, high, dense, any colour.",
    "Two words, since `rings` is the stone formation. Naming them brings them; a word said of the whole Age lands on them only now and then, one Age in ten.",
    "They take no offer left dangling: a stray describing word should not hang rings over an Age.",
    "Density said of the whole Age is how full the land is (`desolate`, `dense`), so it reaches the rings only when aimed at them."
  ],
